SUMMARY:Brandywine Hike
DESCRIPTION:Metrotrails: NJ\, PA\, NY Metropolitan Area Hiking and More!\n
 Join us for this point to point hike\, the next in our series of both the 
 Brandywine Trail and the New Holland Branch of the Pennsylvania Railroad.\
 nWe meet at Sugar's Bridge Nature Area south of Downingtown Pennsylvania a
 t 9\, and shuttle with as few vehicles as possible north to our start poin
 t.\nWe'll begin in Marsh Creek State Park at a point we finished a previou
 s hike in this series.\nThe very beginning will be field edge trails and s
 uch in a newer preserved section. From here\, we will make our way east on
  a very brief road walk to get to where we last left off on the Brandywine
  Trail.\nWe'll pass along the Marsh Creek Lake on this trail\, as well as 
 through woods and farmlands heading to the south.\nWe eventually pass by t
 he dam at Marsh Creek and descend to the Struble Trail\, where we pick up 
 the former New Holland Branch of the Pennsylvania Railroad. The Brandywine
  Trail follows this to Downingtown along the scenic creek.\nWe continue so
 uth and leave the rail bed in Downingtown\, then continue on the creek.\nT
 he pleasant trail ascends through woods after another very brief road bit\
 , and descends again to reach the Brandywine Meadows. From here to the end
 \, we follow an old trolley bed along the creek.\nThis promises to be a gr
 eat hike\, and mostly pretty easy terrain.\nWe will pass places for food i
 n Downingtown.\nDistance will be about 15 miles. If needed\, contact me at
  908 343 8374
